Makor Issues & Rights, Ltd., 551 U.S. 308, 313 (2007). Thus, if Rule 9(b) sets a heightened pleading standard, then the PLSRA sets a super-heightened pleading standard: even the defendant’s state of mind must be stated with “particularity.”



